# Mobile (Expo)

## Runtime

- Use **development builds** (`expo-dev-client`). Expo Go is not the product path.
- Keep Continuous Native Generation: do not commit `ios/` or `android/` unless there is an explicit decision to eject from CNG.
- Rebuild native only after native deps, app config, or SDK changes.

## Data and API

- Call the backend through `@product/client` / contract types.
- No duplicate hand-written API types in the app.
- Auth tokens and session handling follow Better Auth mobile patterns already in the repo — do not invent a parallel auth client.

## UI

- Prefer expo-router file routes already in `app/`.
- Shared visual tokens come from `@product/brand` where applicable — do not fork a second palette.
- Avoid premature `useMemo` / `useCallback` unless profiling or repo convention requires it.

## Visual consistency

A feature folder must not grow its own look. Before adding chrome, find the
screen that already solves the same shape and match it.

- **Display face is rare.** `displayFontFamily` is for one hero numeral or one
  celebration/auth title per screen — the role `streakValue` plays on Home and
  `balanceValue` on Points. Never on a repeating list row, never on every
  screen title in a folder.
- **Lists are divider lists.** Rows sit on `colors.background` separated by a
  `StyleSheet.hairlineWidth` rule in `colors.border`, as in `LeaderboardScreen`
  and `ChallengesScreen`. A `colors.surface` card is for a single emphasised
  block per screen, not the default row container.
- **Row type scale:** `fontSize.sm` title, `fontSize.xs` muted meta.
- **Section labels** are uppercase `fontSize.xs` with `letterSpacing: 0.6`,
  accent for the active step and muted otherwise.
- Do not alias brand tokens behind local constants (`MATCH_CARD_RADIUS` for
  `radii.md`). Use the token.
- Shared chrome lives in a shared folder. If two features need the same row,
  promote it rather than importing across feature folders or copying it.

## Routes

- Every new `app/` route is registered in the root `Stack` in `app/_layout.tsx`
  with `headerShown: false`, and draws its own `DeckPageNav` that leaves via
  `goBackOrHome`. `root-stack-routes.test.ts` fails otherwise; a missing entry
  shows the native "Back / Healthy" header on top of the page's own.
- `router.back()` is a no-op after a deep link; leave a page with `goBackOrHome`.
- Colours come from `theme.colors` keys that exist (`text`, `muted`, …). An
  unknown key is `undefined`, which renders black in dark mode.

## Native camera

- Never snapshot `AVCaptureVideoPreviewLayer` (`render(in:)` draws black).
  Recorded frames come from the capture output via `CameraFrameTap`.
- Proof clips are plain camera footage plus the proof chrome (code, count,
  date). The QuickPose skeleton belongs to the live preview, never the file.
- The server can refuse a publish (for example the daily group cap). Check
  every refusal before any bytes upload, and show the person why in their
  words; a raw or generic error is not done.
- Recording changes are not done until seen on a real device: the clip shows
  the person, plays at real speed, and stays under the contract's size and
  duration caps.

## Release lanes

- JS-only: EAS Update.
- Native changes: store build + review.
- See `docs/releases.md`.
